 3 +6=9, +12=21, +24=45, +30=75, +30=105, +30=135, +30=165. So total would be 165 seconds.\n\nBut wait, the original answer had 61 seconds when retryCount was 5. Now with 8 retries, the sum would be higher. However, the maxDelay is 30, which caps the delays after the fourth attempt. So the delays after n=4 are 30, and the rest are 30. So the sum is 3+6+12+24+30+30+30+30 = 165.\n\nBut I need to check if the retryCount is 8, so n goes from 0 to 7. So the delays are as calculated. Therefore, the total would be 165 seconds.\n\nBut wait, the original problem said that the policy is split across lib/a.dart, lib/b.dart, and the imported file. In the previous scenario, the imported file was lib/c.dart, which had the same settings as lib/a.dart. So the delays for lib/c.dart would be the same as lib/a.dart's delays, which were 3,6,12,20,20. But with retryCount 8, the delays would be 3,6,12,24,30,30,30,30. So the sum is 3+6+12+24+30+30+30+30 = 165.\n\nSo the answer is 165 seconds.\n","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},{"content":[{"annotations":[],"logprobs":[],"text":"The total wait time would be **165 seconds**. \n\n**Breakdown**:\n- **lib/a.dart**: Delays are 3, 6, 12, 24, 30, 30, 30, 30 → sum = 165  \n- **lib/b.dart**: No delay settings (not included)  \n- **lib/c.dart**: Same as lib/a.dart (since it's the imported file)  \n\n**Total**: 3 + 6 + 12 + 24 + 30 + 30 + 30 + 30 = **165 seconds**.","type":"output_text"}],"id":"msg_493728","role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message"}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"presence_penalty":0,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"reasoning":null,"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"default","status":"completed","store":false,"temperature":1,"text":{"format":{"type":"text"}},"tool_choice":"auto","tools":[{"description":"Read one text file of the repository at the pinned commit.","name":"read_file","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"path":{"description":"Repository-relative path, 